meta {
  name: Get Duplicate Rule - Match Conditions
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{CRM_URL}}/duplicaterules({{duplicateRuleId}})?$expand=DuplicateRule_DuplicateRuleConditions
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  $expand: DuplicateRule_DuplicateRuleConditions
}

vars:pre-request {
  duplicateRuleId: 2b79a040-ccd5-ec11-a7b5-000d3adcba42
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Reveals what "Look for Active Amend Bank Cases by SBI" actually matches
  on: casetypecode (new incident's case type = an existing incident's case
  type) AND rpa_organisation (same organisation), excludeinactiverecords:
  true. Despite the name, this is not scoped to a specific case type value —
  it fires for ANY two active incidents sharing the same case type and
  organisation, which structurally includes two document-upload cases from
  the same SBI submitted close together. The relationship name
  (DuplicateRule_DuplicateRuleConditions) was found via "Discover Duplicate
  Rule Relationship Names" after guessing the wrong name first.
}
